Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Post-merge mutation check of #2429/#2481 (card t_01a1d615bdcca774) found four mutants that the 68 tests in
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py + tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py let
survive. One test per mutant, tests only:

- C2 `_NEGATED.search(before[ends[-1] ...:])` -> `_NEGATED.search(before)`: `\s+` crosses a newline, so the
  "not" of "Tests: not run" would deny "Duplicate of t_X" on the next line.
  test_a_negator_ending_the_previous_line_does_not_deny_the_next_line
- C7' `(?:not|never|` -> `(?:not|`: test_never_denies_the_keyword ("Never a duplicate of t_X." -> []).
- C10 `n['\u2019]t` -> `n[']t`: test_a_contraction_with_a_typographic_apostrophe_denies_the_keyword
  ("Isn’t a duplicate of t_X." -> []).
- D2' `mine_m and their_m` -> `(mine_m or their_m)` in `enumerated`: fail-open, a replaced span with a
  marker on one side only ("Fix guard at 9baf8d8abc follow-up" vs "Fix guard cleanup follow-up") would read
  as an enumeration and admit a same-creator duplicate.
  test_a_replaced_span_with_a_marker_on_one_side_only_is_not_an_enumeration (both directions).

Proof: on origin/main all 73 tests pass; under each mutant exactly its new test fails (C2/C7'/C10: 1 failed,
D2': 2 failed). Same result with these tests applied on top of open PR #2535 (wt/overlap-guard-nits-t01a1d62c),
which edits the same guards; the new tests are appended at the file ends so the two merge cleanly.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py       | 14 ++++++++++++++
 .../test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py     | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py
index d33f9442ae..6c92c66c10 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py
@@ -162,3 +162,17 @@ def test_a_closed_detector_card_lets_the_next_occurrence_open_a_new_one(conn):
     third = kb.create_task(conn, title="third", assignee="default", creator_task_id=creator)
     assert kb.complete_task(conn, third, summary=f"Superseded by {first}.")
     assert len(dd.describe(conn)) == 2
+
+
+def test_a_negator_ending_the_previous_line_does_not_deny_the_next_line():
+    """A newline ends the clause: the "not" of "Tests: not run" does not deny the duplicate on the next line."""
+    assert dd.sibling_named("Tests: not run\nDuplicate of t_0123456789abcdef.") == ["t_0123456789abcdef"]
+
+
+def test_never_denies_the_keyword():
+    assert dd.sibling_named("Never a duplicate of t_0123456789abcdef.") == []
+
+
+def test_a_contraction_with_a_typographic_apostrophe_denies_the_keyword():
+    """U+2019, as pasted from rendered markdown, denies like the ASCII apostrophe."""
+    assert dd.sibling_named("Isn\u2019t a duplicate of t_0123456789abcdef.") == []
diff --git a/tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py b/tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py
index 407087ec43..3c93cad892 100644
--- a/tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py
+++ b/tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py
@@ -208,3 +208,15 @@ def test_worker_enumerated_legs_and_distinct_override_still_create(worker):
     second = _tool_create(title=NIT + " (round 2)", distinct_from=[first["task_id"]],
                           distinct_reason="round-2 nits are separate")
     assert second["ok"] and second.get("created", True) and second["task_id"] != first["task_id"]
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("mine, theirs", [
+    ("Fix guard at 9baf8d8abc follow-up", "Fix guard cleanup follow-up"),
+    ("Fix guard cleanup follow-up", "Fix guard at 9baf8d8abc follow-up"),
+])
+def test_a_replaced_span_with_a_marker_on_one_side_only_is_not_an_enumeration(mine, theirs):
+    """Only a marker on both sides of a replaced span is an index: a sha that replaced a word is a re-issue."""
+    from hermes_cli import kanban_overlap_own as own
+    card = {"title": theirs, "assignee": "default"}
+    assert own.enumerated(mine, theirs) is None
+    assert own.own_distinct(mine, "default", card) is None
